From 8f897e05aea7f23b3d7d2dfd86a8e4a4ae71b388 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sjcsf <346224915+llsf2020@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] FreeChat: join private rooms with a password;
 admin-only privacy settings

- Room admins set a join password (argon2 hash stored server-side only,
  never in room state); anyone with the room link and password is invited
  on behalf of a member who can invite, then joins normally. Five wrong
  attempts lock a user out of that room for 15 minutes; missing rooms and
  wrong passwords answer identically.
- com.freechat.privacy {block_screenshots} is admin-only like the TTL and
  always returned by sliding sync.
